{"title":"Orcish Grip Wrap","html":"<article class=\"wp\"><div class=\"wp-main\">\n      <p class=\"wp-lede\">Monster drop: Orc Berserker, Orc Grunt</p>\n      \n      \n      \n      \n      <h2>What it’s for</h2><p>Every gem transmuter has a <b>Reagent</b> tab, the Dark Witch included. This reagent and <b>500 gold</b> get you a gem of a random kind of <b>1c, 1.5c or 2c</b>. Monsters no longer drop reagents.</p><p class=\"muted\">See <a href=\"#/guide/reagents\">Reagents</a>.</p>\n      <h2>How to get it</h2>\n      \n      \n      \n      \n      \n      <div style=\"margin-top:10px\"><b>Recorded monster drops</b><div class=\"chip-row\"><div class=\"entity-chip monsterlink\" data-monster=\"orc-berserker\" title=\"Orc Berserker - dropped it in 1 of 20 looted corpses (1/20)\"><img class=\"thumb monsterthumb\" src=\"data/img/fd2890ecfdd2a50fb876.webp\" alt=\"\"><span class=\"entity-chip-label\">Orc Berserker</span><span class=\"entity-chip-stat\">1/20<br>×1</span></div><div class=\"entity-chip monsterlink\" data-monster=\"orc-grunt\" title=\"Orc Grunt - dropped it in 1 of 25 looted corpses (1/25)\"><img class=\"thumb monsterthumb\" src=\"data/img/9c694d24818e1e184cda.webp\" alt=\"\"><span class=\"entity-chip-label\">Orc Grunt</span><span class=\"entity-chip-stat\">1/25<br>×1</span></div></div><div class=\"s muted\" style=\"margin-top:6px\">Drop rate as 1/X (about 1 kill in X drops it, counted over the corpses of each monster whose loot was recorded), and ×N, how many come in one drop.</div></div>\n      <button type=\"button\" class=\"show-on-map\" data-map-kind=\"item\" data-map-id=\"orcish-grip-wrap\">Show where to get it on the map</button>\n      \n      \n      \n      \n      \n    </div><aside class=\"wp-infobox\"><div class=\"wp-pic \"><img src=\"data/img/7a02dc5ba2daa9da8cc8.svg\" alt=\"Orcish Grip Wrap\"></div><h3>Orcish Grip Wrap</h3><table>\n      \n      \n      \n      \n      <tr><th>Dropped by</th><td>2 monsters</td></tr>\n      \n      \n      <tr><th>Last seen</th><td>11/2/2026, 2:23:30 PM</td></tr>\n    </table></aside></article>"}